{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And I will visit upon you.</b> And I will decree upon you." "<b>Consumption.</b> An illness that consumes the flesh, אנפו\"ליש בלעז; it resembles a swelling, except that its puffing is lighter and the appearance of its face is gaunt." "<b>Burning fever.</b> An illness that scorches the body and heats it and burns it, as in ״כִּי אֵשׁ קָדְחָה בְאַפִּי״ (Deuteronomy 32)." "<b>Consuming the eyes and wasting the soul.</b> The eyes gaze and pine to see that it lighten and heal — but in the end it does not heal, and the souls of his family waste away at his death; every desire that goes unfulfilled and a prolonged hope is called כִלְיוֹן עֵינַיִם." "<b>And you shall sow in vain.</b> You shall sow and it shall not sprout — and if it sprouts, <b>your enemies shall eat it.</b>"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French enfler, 'to inflate/swell'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:39.617968908Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}